00:38:23.799 --> 00:38:30.267
We find out by studying Quran carefully that
he contributed all religious practices of Islam.

00:38:30.267 --> 00:38:33.848
The prophet Muhammad contributed the Quran.

00:38:34.094 --> 00:38:37.573
The Quran came through Muhammad's mouth,
and that was his contribution.

00:38:38.233 --> 00:38:46.795
And this is also why at the beginning of Sura Al-Baqarah, number 2, we find that we must believe in what was revealed before the Quran.

00:38:47.267 --> 00:38:53.845
Because among the things revealed before
Quran was the practical scripture given to Ibrahim.

00:38:53.845 --> 00:38:57.119
There was no reading or writing in Ibrahim's
time.

00:38:57.119 --> 00:39:06.246
Dr. Khalifa: And he was given a practical, mostly practical,
scripture consisting of the duties that we practice now in Islam.

00:39:10.000 --> 00:39:11.339
Ray Caton: Question number 7.

00:39:11.717 --> 00:39:18.012
Ray Caton: There are two verses in Quran, Sura 60, 7, 8 and 9.

00:39:18.484 --> 00:39:22.372
Sura 5, 85 and 82.

00:39:22.608 --> 00:39:30.413
Ray Caton: Basically, these refer to the believer not
trusting the Jews ...

00:39:32.678 --> 00:39:34.961
Dr. Khalifa: Not befriending the Christians and Jews and so forth.

00:39:34.961 --> 00:39:38.140
Ray Caton: Yes. The question that was asked is

00:39:38.140 --> 00:39:47.361
"whether or not a person who is a believing Muslim should live in a country that is suppressing Islam,

00:39:47.361 --> 00:39:52.523
"and supporting that country by paying taxes,
creating business, employment, one thing or another.

00:39:52.523 --> 00:40:00.000
Ray Caton: "Should he stay there, live, or should he move
to another better environment, a more Islamic environment?"

00:40:01.465 --> 00:40:12.758
Dr. Khalifa: Well, if the person is oppressed and cannot practice his religion, he cannot Pray, he cannot Fast, he cannot give to charity, and cannot go to hajj, he should move on to another place.

00:40:13.230 --> 00:40:15.230
But this is about the only condition.

00:40:16.646 --> 00:40:28.227
To say "you shall not befriend Christians and Jews, and that the Quran says so" would be like saying "you shall not Pray, because
the Quran says you shall not pray."

00:40:29.029 --> 00:40:33.294
However, if you complete the sentence, it
will say "you shall not Pray while drunk."

00:40:33.860 --> 00:40:37.418
And the same with that statement "you shall
not befriend the Jews and Christians",

00:40:37.418 --> 00:40:46.450
it should be, the sentence or the statement should be completed as follows "you shall not befriend the Jews and Christians who oppress you and persecute you because of your religion."

00:40:47.913 --> 00:40:51.329
Towards the end of Sura number 60, which
you mentioned,

00:40:51.329 --> 00:41:00.409
specifically the Quran says that God does not forbid you from befriending those who do not fight you and do not evict you from your homes.

00:41:00.787 --> 00:41:10.669
So, we must take the total picture in mind, and we must never tell half-truths or half-statements of Quran. It's very dangerous.

00:41:11.235 --> 00:41:17.908
So, we are not, God does not forbid us from
befriending the Jews, Christians, or anyone else who do not fight us.

00:41:22.581 --> 00:41:26.752
Dr. Khalifa: What other parts of the question, I have something
else to say, I know that.

00:41:27.554 --> 00:41:29.554
Ray Caton: It's whether or not a person should stay...
Dr. Khalifa: Oh, yes.

00:41:29.554 --> 00:41:34.905
Dr. Khalifa: About staying in a country, for example,
some people say that this country is not Islamic or oppressive,

00:41:34.905 --> 00:41:41.342
talking about the United States, but in my mind, the United States is about the most Islamic country in the world,

00:41:41.342 --> 00:41:47.353
because a person
is free to worship God in any way they want,

00:41:47.353 --> 00:41:54.923
to the extent that if you, if you are in Egypt, or
Saudi Arabia, or one of those countries, and you

00:41:54.923 --> 00:42:02.775
really speak up for the true Islam, which is upholding Quran, the whole Quran, nothing but Quran, your life is actually endangered.

00:42:03.483 --> 00:42:12.610
So, it seems to me that the United States is
a lot more Islamic than Saudi Arabia, by using that measure.

00:42:13.507 --> 00:42:23.295
Dr. Khalifa: So, people who think that this country is oppressing
or, or hampering their Islam in any way, they should think twice.

00:42:25.295 --> 00:42:31.307
Ray Caton: Question number eight, what is the importance
of three times washing as opposed to wash till clean?

00:42:31.732 --> 00:42:34.818
Dr. Khalifa: Oh, it's not important, there is no specific
number.

00:42:35.290 --> 00:42:46.824
The Quran says "O you who believe, when you get up to Pray, wash your faces, your hands to the elbows, wipe your hair, and wash your feet, that's it, there is no specific number of washings.

00:42:47.532 --> 00:42:52.552
Dr. Khalifa: One will do 2, may do, whichever you feel
is necessary.

00:42:54.298 --> 00:42:57.431
Ray Caton: Question number nine "does it do any good
to pray for the dead?"

00:42:57.620 --> 00:43:07.266
Dr. Khalifa: No, it all depends on the person's deeds, the dead person, whatever he or she did during this life is what counts.

00:43:08.116 --> 00:43:14.175
If the whole world bands together to pray
for Abu Lahab, it will not help him one bit.

00:43:15.402 --> 00:43:22.075
Dr. Khalifa: And if a person is righteous, his righteousness
will benefit him.

00:43:24.482 --> 00:43:33.609
Ray Caton: Number eleven, the word Riba (Usury), meaning interest,
does this mean excessive interest or just interest?

00:43:34.081 --> 00:43:39.479
Dr. Khalifa: Any interest that is fixed and guaranteed
is considered usury, Riba,

00:43:39.479 --> 00:43:45.680
but if it fluctuates as a result of investing, then this is what
is Halal, what is alright.

00:43:46.624 --> 00:43:54.193
Dr. Khalifa: So, the key thing here is fixed and guaranteed,
this makes it Riba even if it's 1%, 10% whatever.

00:43:57.119 --> 00:44:04.169
Ray Caton: So, while we are on the subject of money, could
you expand a little bit on mortgage and insurance?

00:44:04.169 --> 00:44:11.691
Dr. Khalifa: So, the Quran, the Quran is consistent in saying that it
is the taking of Riba that is Haram,

00:44:11.691 --> 00:44:21.149
when you take interest, it is Haram, but if you
are forced by circumstances to pay interest to anybody,

00:44:21.149 --> 00:44:27.019
you are considered a victim, the
Quran considers you a victim, you're not committing a sin.

00:44:28.576 --> 00:44:37.136
There's the overall rule that says "if you are forced by circumstances without being deliberate or malicious, then you are not committing a sin."

00:44:37.514 --> 00:44:40.364
So, if you are forced to pay interest, that
is not Haram.

00:44:40.364 --> 00:44:46.517
What is Haram, consistently in Quran,
is the taking of Riba, not the paying of Riba.

00:44:48.311 --> 00:44:56.399
Insurance is considered Haram because of many
reasons, first of all, it is a game of chance, gambling.

00:44:57.862 --> 00:45:04.818
Second, it indicates lack of knowledge about
God, because if you know,

00:45:04.818 --> 00:45:10.499
then you'll know that if you, if you are with God, nothing bad will
happen to you, God will take care of you.

00:45:10.688 --> 00:45:12.452
(39:36) أَلَيْسَ ٱللَّهُ بِكَافٍ عَبْدَهُۥ

00:45:12.452 --> 00:45:14.688
[39:36]  Is GOD not sufficient for His servant? ...

00:45:15.254 --> 00:45:19.378
And also, insurance indicates lack of confidence
in God.

00:45:20.841 --> 00:45:24.115
So, there is more to it than just a game of chance.

00:45:25.389 --> 00:45:31.118
However, if you are forced, again, if you
are forced by circumstance without being deliberate or malicious,

00:45:31.118 --> 00:45:37.224
Dr. Khalifa: and you cannot help it, you have to have insurance for some reason, or it is forced on you, then you are not committing a sin.

00:45:38.734 --> 00:45:45.973
Ray Caton: Just to broaden the question a bit more on
mortgage, in terms of loans,

00:45:45.973 --> 00:45:55.855
if a person wants to gain more material wealth by expanding his business and goes into debt by borrowing money to expand his business,

00:45:55.855 --> 00:46:03.377
Ray Caton: to the point where you might call it excessive, greedy, is this allowable?

00:46:04.557 --> 00:46:16.988
Dr. Khalifa: If you write down a project that you want to build apartment complex or invest in something, and to do this you have to have a loan of some kind,

00:46:16.988 --> 00:46:24.180
and then, you go to the bank or a friend or anybody, any source of
money, and they tell you "you have to pay interest."

00:46:25.454 --> 00:46:33.071
However, if you take the loan, you know that you will make this investment grow and will bring you a lot of income and a lot of money,

00:46:33.071 --> 00:46:40.877
it is perfectly alright that you go ahead and get the loan and invest it and make your money grow and pay the interest,

00:46:40.877 --> 00:46:50.759
because in Sura 16, we see that the Quran very clearly
says that the rich believer is better than the weak and poor believer.

00:46:51.231 --> 00:46:56.204
It is in Satan's best interest to keep you, keep you poor

00:46:56.204 --> 00:47:05.425
and unable to further the cause of God in any way, or increase your knowledge in any way, or benefit from God's provisions.

00:47:05.619 --> 00:47:15.579
So, it is perfectly alright if you write down a project that requires a lot of money to be invested, that will make you a lot of money, make you a millionaire, or whatever.

00:47:16.516 --> 00:47:22.638
Dr. Khalifa: It is perfectly alright to get that loan
and pay the interest on it, and invest and carry out your project.

00:47:25.659 --> 00:47:26.857
